Hi.  Lars Huttar here, with a request for help with termcap.c,
on Apollos.

Symptom of bug: none of the terminal-control (e.g. cursor movement)
strings are output.  So of course the arrangment of stuff on the screen
is all wrong.

Narrowing it down:  using dbx, I've found that the strings being passed
to tputs() are fine.  Nice, healthy strings like "^[[h" or whatever.
tputs() is supposed to do some stuff like padding and output the appropriate
characters using xputc().  But it turns out that the only characters xputc()
is getting are nulls ('\0').

A hack: so I tried bypassing tputs, just using fputs.  Well, that works on
fast terminals, like an xterm, but if I rlogin from a 2400-baud terminal
I get quite a bit of additional screen garbage -- mostly 2's, 3's and 5's.

Request: does anybody know how to make tputs() happy on Apollos?
By the way I did check that ospeed was getting set to the proper value.
This in the BSD environment; Domain/OS Version SR10.3.  Using native cc,
etc.  nethack pl9.  Not entirely pure; I have made a few changes, but nothing
that should affect the termcap stuff, I'm quite sure.

